.TH MU2ECOMPILER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2eCompiler \- compile a CFO run-plan source file to binary (fixed paths)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2eCompiler
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs
.B CFOLib::CFO_Compiler::processFile()
on the hard-coded input
.I /home/mu2ehwdev/ots/srcs/mu2e_pcie_utils/cfoInterfaceLib/Commands.txt
and writes
.IR .../Commands.bin
in the same directory.
Command-line arguments are ignored: the argument parser
.RB ( setIOFiles() ,
which handled
.BR \-\-help ,
.B \-\-new
and
.I "infile outfile"
operands) is defined but never called.
The instruction language (SET_TAG, LOOP/DO_LOOP, HEARTBEAT, MARKER, WAIT, INC_TAG,
END, ...) is described in
.I cfoInterfaceLib/README.txt
and the example
.IR Commands.txt ,
installed under the package data directory.
.PP
To compile an arbitrary file use
.B cfoUtil \-C \-p
.I in
.B \-f
.I out
.BR write_program .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; failures inside the compiler are reported on stdout.
.SH FILES
.I /home/mu2ehwdev/ots/srcs/mu2e_pcie_utils/cfoInterfaceLib/Commands.txt
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
cfoUtil \-C \-p myplan.txt \-f myplan.bin write_program
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cfoUtil (1),
.BR libCFOInterface (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
